-                    + replace(value.substring(end), key, replaceValue);
+        // Iterative left-to-right, non-overlapping replacement. Each occurrence
+        // of key in the ORIGINAL value is replaced with replaceValue; text just
+        // appended from replaceValue is never rescanned for further key
+        // occurrences, because the scan cursor (start) advances through the
+        // original value only. Stack usage is O(1) regardless of the number of
+        // occurrences, so no value can drive the JVM stack to exhaustion
+        // (CWE-674 / CWE-400 / CWE-770).
+        final int keyLength = key.length();
